CAT = "pknleCommForensic"; SEG = "CFM"
Q = [
("A screening test detects 90 of 100 people who have a disease. What does this figure describe?",
 "Sensitivity of 90%", ["Specificity of 90%", "Positive predictive value", "Prevalence of 90%"],
 "Sensitivity is true positives divided by everyone with the disease: 90 of 100. Specificity is about people without the disease."),
("In a trial, 12% of untreated patients and 8% of treated patients have a stroke. What is the number needed to treat?",
 "25", ["4", "33", "12"],
 "Absolute risk reduction is 12% minus 8% = 4%, or 0.04. The number needed to treat is 1 divided by 0.04 = 25."),
("Which study design starts with people who have a disease and people who do not, then looks back at exposures?",
 "Case-control study", ["Cohort study", "Randomised trial", "Cross-sectional survey"],
 "A case-control study compares past exposure in cases and controls and yields an odds ratio. A cohort study follows exposed and unexposed people forward."),
('After a wedding dinner, 54 of 180 guests develop vomiting and diarrhoea. What is the attack rate?',
 '30%', ['43%', '18%', '54%'],
 'Attack rate is the number of new cases divided by the population at risk: 54 / 180 = 0.30, or 30%. Dividing by the 126 who stayed well gives the wrong 43%.'),
("Which community worker in Pakistan provides family planning, antenatal visits and child health care at household level?",
 "Lady Health Worker", ["Sanitary inspector", "Dispenser at a BHU", "Union council secretary"],
 "The Lady Health Worker programme places trained women from the community to serve households with maternal, child and family planning care, linked to a health facility."),
("How much contact time does chlorine need with water to disinfect it?",
 "At least 30 minutes", ["About 1 minute", "About 5 minutes", "At least 24 hours"],
 "WHO technical notes say chlorine needs at least 30 minutes of contact, and residual chlorine where people collect water should be 0.2 to 0.5 mg/L; much higher levels taste bad."),
("Rigor mortis usually appears first in which muscles?",
 "Eyelids and jaw", ["The lower limbs", "The trunk and back", "The toes and feet"],
 "Rigor follows Nysten's rule, starting in small muscles of the eyelids and jaw about 1 to 2 hours after death and spreading down to the limbs."),
("In a gunshot entry wound, what does a ring of tattooing around the hole indicate?",
 "Close but not contact range", ["Shot from a long distance", "Exit, not entry wound", "Firm contact with the skin"],
 "Unburnt powder grains embed in the skin when the muzzle is close enough for them to reach it, but not touching. Contact wounds show soot and searing in the wound edges instead."),
("A body recovered from a canal shows fine froth at the mouth and nostrils. What does this suggest?",
 "Drowning while alive", ["Death before immersion", "Hanging before immersion", "Long period in the water"],
 "Persistent fine froth comes from air mixing with water and mucus in breathing lungs, a sign of ante-mortem drowning. Diatoms in the bone marrow support it."),
("In hanging, which feature of the ligature mark helps tell it from strangulation?",
 "Oblique, rising to the knot", ["Horizontal, all round the neck", "Below the thyroid cartilage", "With fingernail marks nearby"],
 "A hanging mark runs obliquely upwards towards the suspension point and is often incomplete. A ligature strangulation mark is usually horizontal and complete, lower on the neck."),
("Under the Pakistan Penal Code, a head injury that exposes the bone without fracturing it is called:",
 "Shajjah-i-mudihah", ["Shajjah-i-khafifah", "Shajjah-i-hashimah", "Shajjah-i-munaqqilah"],
 "Section 337 classes head and face injuries: khafifah does not expose bone, mudihah exposes it without fracture, hashimah fractures it and munaqqilah fractures and dislocates it."),
("A young man is brought in after swallowing a 'wheat pill', a fumigant tablet kept in stored grain. He has severe shock that does not respond to fluids. What is the poison?",
 "Aluminium phosphide", ["Barium carbonate", "Copper sulphate", "Organophosphate"],
 "Aluminium phosphide grain tablets release phosphine gas in the stomach, causing refractory shock. There is no specific antidote, so care is supportive."),
]
